# Verify work twice (mandatory)

After finishing any implementation, wiring, or doc update: **do not claim done until you have verified the work twice.** Shipping unverified code is a process failure.

## When this applies

- API client changes, page/tab wires, adapters, forms, creates/writes
- Backend-asks / gap docs that claim FE or BE closure
- Any task where the user asked for a feature to work end-to-end

## Pass 1 — Static / consistency check

Re-read the changed files (not just memory of the edit):

1. Symbols used in UI exist on the API client (method names, args).
2. No leftover local `setState` / seed / mock / “Create locally” on paths claimed live.
3. Imports resolve; callbacks match prop names (`onComplete` vs `onOrderCreated`, etc.).
4. Gap/asks docs match reality if you updated status to “wired”.

## Pass 2 — Evidence check

Prove the wire path with at least one of:

1. Grep that the live call site invokes the API (not a stub), **or**
2. Trace one happy path: user action → client method → expected endpoint, **or**
3. If the workspace allows, run a focused typecheck/lint on touched files and fix failures you introduced.

If Pass 2 fails, **fix before responding**. Do not ask the user to discover broken wires.

## Response rule

Only say “done / wired / live” after both passes. If something is unverified or blocked, say so explicitly (file + what was not checked).

## Anti-patterns

```text
❌ Edit UI → mark gaps “FE wired” → stop
❌ “Should work” without re-reading call sites
❌ Parallel subagents finished → trust summary with no parent verify

✅ Edit → Pass 1 re-read → Pass 2 grep/trace → then report
```
